 CONSTRAINTS block on WORK_ASSIGNMENT dispatch

FR-4: adds stampConstraintsBlock, a fourth fail-soft stamper guard at
insertCoordinationRow (buildWorkAssignment does not exist anywhere in
the repo -- the real choke point already runs three sibling stampers).
Renders the target SD's ratifications_cited, resolvable hold (via
FR-3's widened resolveHoldProvenance), and any recorded Solomon-ruling
text into a CONSTRAINTS block, writing BOTH row.body and
row.payload.body directly so the existing two fill-if-absent body
mirrors can never desynchronize the two copies.

Fails soft on an oversized render: capBodySafe never throws, so an
over-cap CONSTRAINTS block is dropped with a warning and the
un-stamped WORK_ASSIGNMENT still inserts, matching the sibling
stampers' contract.

