Subject: [PATCH 08/10] 
 fix(SD-LEO-INFRA-COORDINATOR-RECEIPTS-BROADCAST-CONSTRAINTS-001): stop
 widening the shared resolveHoldProvenance

EXEC-phase TESTING (evidence 4298bd82) found that widening the
shared resolveHoldProvenance with 4 new keys had an unaudited
fleet-wide consequence: scripts/post-merge-handoff-orchestrator.js's
classifyState() and lib/fleet/belt-census.cjs both gate real
behavior on whatever this function resolves, and the widening moved
64 live SDs into a newly-resolved hold, 11 non-terminal, stalling
their auto-handoff -- permanently, since none of the 4 keys had a
release-check path.

Reverts resolveHoldProvenance to its original 6-key precedence chain
and removes the HOLD_REASON_KEYS export. FR-3's actual intent
(surface human_action_note/human_action_reason/human_action_required/
needs_coordinator_review_reason to the worker) is achieved instead by
having stampConstraintsBlock read these four keys DIRECTLY -- a
descriptive-only surface with zero effect on any dispatch/handoff/
belt gate, the same pattern already used for the solomon_* fields.

Removes the two test files whose premise (a widened shared resolver)
no longer holds, adds a regression guard confirming the 4 keys stay
unresolved by resolveHoldProvenance, and adds explicit stampConstraints
Block coverage for all 4 keys at their new direct-read site.

