Subject: [PATCH 09/10] 
 docs(SD-LEO-INFRA-COORDINATOR-RECEIPTS-BROADCAST-CONSTRAINTS-001): correct
 stale dead-letter gauge comment (REG-1)

REGRESSION (reg-receipts-verify, evidence 87335241) found that
signal_receipt and capped_pool_broadcast's deliberate dual
membership (informational-by-precedence yet also drain-set-owned via
BACKPRESSURE_EXEMPT_KINDS) makes this else-branch's blanket "no
DRAIN_SET ever owns this kind" comment factually false for these two
kinds. The bucketing behavior itself is unchanged and directionally
correct; only the comment risked a future mis-triage of a real
delivery gap as pure structural noise for these two kinds
specifically.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01XjY63pandj5ZCUyK795C4H

Fleet-Worker: Alpha-3
Claude-Session: a13f0a2c-1450-4259-9c75-de5009ca906a
---
 lib/coordination/lane-dead-letter-gauge.cjs | 9 +++++++++
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+)

diff --git a/lib/coordination/lane-dead-letter-gauge.cjs b/lib/coordination/lane-dead-letter-gauge.cjs
index e3a124cacc..f7efec4cb9 100644
--- a/lib/coordination/lane-dead-letter-gauge.cjs
+++ b/lib/coordination/lane-dead-letter-gauge.cjs
@@ -78,6 +78,15 @@ function summarizeLaneDeadLetterRates(rows, { nowMs = Date.now() } = {}) {
       } else {
         // 'unrecognized'/'informational': no DRAIN_SET ever owns this kind, so read_at was
         // structurally never going to be stamped -- not a real delivery failure (TS-6).
+        // EXCEPTION (REG-1, SD-LEO-INFRA-COORDINATOR-RECEIPTS-BROADCAST-CONSTRAINTS-001):
+        // signal_receipt and capped_pool_broadcast are DELIBERATE dual-membership kinds --
+        // informational by classification precedence (lib/fleet/worker-status.cjs
+        // INFORMATIONAL_KINDS is checked before the drain-set union), yet ALSO owned by every
+        // role's DRAIN_SET via the BACKPRESSURE_EXEMPT_KINDS spread. An expired-unread instance
+        // of one of these two kinds specifically COULD have been read/acked and was not, so it
+        // falls in this bucket by classification but is not "structurally" artifact-prone the
+        // way a genuinely-ownerless kind is -- read the finer-grained per-kind breakdown before
+        // triaging a rate change on either of these two kinds as pure structural noise.
         bucket.structurally_artifact_prone += 1;
       }
     }

