 fix(SD-LEO-INFRA-COORDINATOR-RECEIPTS-BROADCAST-CONSTRAINTS-001): wire
 countUnreceiptedOverdue into the gauge registry (FR-5(d))

VALIDATION (val-receipts-verify, evidence 644cb7c8) found
countUnreceiptedOverdue had no production caller anywhere and was
absent from lib/governance/gauge-registry.js, so FR-5(d)'s stated
purpose ("asserted at zero from the merge commit") was not
operational -- it only passed at the fixture level.

Registers a new 'unreceipted-signals-overdue' gauge entry, wired
through a new scripts/gauge-runner.mjs resolver that calls
fetchAllOutstandingSignals + countUnreceiptedOverdue. The shaping
function maps the gauge's 'unknown' state (a lookup failure) to
count:1 rather than a falsy 0, so an unverified read trips the
registry's generic tripWhen convention instead of silently reading
as healthy -- the same false-pass-0 contract AC-15 already tests at
the pure-function level.

Also corrects a docblock at dispatch.cjs:713 that still said
resolveHoldProvenance was "widened by FR-3", contradicting the
revert documented 15 lines below it.

